# Provider transport and proxy boundary

Every outbound request belonging to an LLM provider — completions, streams,
model discovery, account usage, OAuth/device sign-in, token refresh, revoke,
and any provider added later — must follow that row's `providers[].proxy`
setting.

- Production provider helpers accept the row's proxy setting and build their
  client through `llm.HTTPClientForProviderProxy`; do not use
  `http.DefaultClient`, `&http.Client{}`, `http.Get`, `http.Post`, or
  `http.Head` in a provider path.
- A helper that needs a custom `*http.Client` only as a test seam must reject
  `nil`; nil must never silently fall back to a direct/environment client.
- Settings sign-in starts before Save. If the form carries an unsaved `proxy`,
  apply it after resolving the row, including when the saved row has another
  provider type. An absent field retains the row value; `""` / `inherit`
  inherit the process proxy; `none` goes direct; invalid settings return 400.
- When changing provider transport, extend `features/provider_proxy.feature`
  and `internal/llm/bdd_provider_proxy_test.go` for every new request class,
  and keep `TestProviderProxyGuard` green.
